[scene name="BeerLambert" version=1]
; Beer-Lambert thick-glass absorption test. Two identically-sized glass spheres
; over a checker wall, both with the SAME green attenuationColor. The only
; difference is refractionDistance (the thick lens's authored path length): the
; LEFT sphere is thin (0.3), the RIGHT is thick (1.2). If Beer-Lambert works, the
; RIGHT sphere reads visibly deeper green / darker than the LEFT - distance-
; dependent volume absorption, not a flat tint. The checker outside the spheres
; is the un-absorbed reference.

